<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buguma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buguma is a town in Rivers State in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amanyanabo">Amanyanabo</a> of Kalabari. It was founded in the early 1880s by Kalabari people who left their old capital, Elem Kalabari, after a civil war and conflict with the Bonny Kingdom. It remains the political centre of the Kalabari, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abonnema">Abonnema</a> and Bakana.</p></div>
